   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The function f is defined by f(x) = (x + 3) / (x^2 - 1) for x < 2 and f(x) = 40 / (3x(6 - x)) for x >= 2. On how many separate maximal intervals is f continuous?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 4
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "On x < 2 the first rule is undefined at x = -1 and x = 1. On x >= 2 the second rule is undefined only at x = 6, since its other zero x = 0 lies outside that piece.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               1
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               1
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Each rule is rational and so continuous on its own domain. At the join, the left limit (2 + 3) / (4 - 1) = 5/3 equals f(2) = 40 / 24 = 5/3, so f is continuous at x = 2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            5,
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "f is continuous on (-infinity, -1), (-1, 1), (1, 6) and (6, infinity).",
         "mathjson": 6
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Those are four separate maximal intervals.",
         "mathjson": 4
      }
   ],
